% ============================================================================
% Headline 1: Governance conflict error predicate  [EXERCISED 2026-07-28 + 2026-08-03, check -k]
% ============================================================================
% Fires when a credential carries all three governance mandates -- eIDAS
% mandate, privacy requirement, and VCDM-conformance mandate -- and no single
% format satisfies them jointly.
%
% MINIMALITY: SUPERSEDED 2026-08-05. This header previously argued that gating
% on all three annotations (DEC-governance_conflict_triple_gate_and_taxonomy_count) makes the triple conjunction minimal,
% because every proper subset (G0-G6) was SAT. That reading was circular: all
% three clauses below require all three annotation targets at once, so the
% G0-G6 verdicts were entailed by this predicate's syntax and said nothing
% about format availability. C5, C6 and C7 are now encoded independently, one
% rule set per governance source, in governance_sources.refinery. Under that
% encoding the conflict is NOT minimal at the triple: G4 {eIDAS, privacy} and
% G6 {privacy, VCDM} are both UNSAT, G5 {eIDAS, VCDM} is SAT. The two minimal
% conflicting provision sets are the two pairs containing the GDPR privacy
% requirement. Verbatim verdicts: vault ART-constraint_sensitivity_variants,
% block "2026-08-05 -- G0-G7 under independent per-source C5/C6/C7".
%
% Status (re-exercised 2026-08-05 with refinery-cli check -k, image digest
% sha256:88f1332e9aae356d91aef86aaaa3368be1b3931929fb3e10d87d65ab8a7fca8e):
%   - csok.problem / csok_2x.problem / csok_3x.problem -> UNSAT, still carrying
%     "governance_conflict::governance_conflict(IncomeCred, income_format):
%     error." (one atom per income credential at 2x/3x), now alongside the
%     per-source atoms from governance_sources.
%   - evaluation/instances/sensitivity_G0/G1/G2/G3/G5.problem -> "Model is
%     consistent" (SAT).
%   - evaluation/instances/sensitivity_G4/G6/G7.problem -> UNSAT.
%
% This predicate is retained: it is the credential-granularity diagnostic that
% names the joint conflict in one atom. It is no longer what makes the CSOK
% instance unsatisfiable -- C5 and C6 alone already do that -- so it must not
% be described as the sole carrier of the UNSAT verdict.
%
% The three clauses partition the failure condition
%   !(conforms_vcdm(f) & supports_predicate_proof(f)):
%   Clause 1: VCDM-conformant, but no predicate proofs (SD-JWT-VC, JSON-LD, JWT-VC).
%   Clause 2: predicate-proof-capable, but not VCDM-conformant (AnonCreds).
%   Clause 3: neither VCDM-conformant nor predicate-proof-capable (mdoc).
% No deployed format is both, so every format triggers a clause -> UNSAT.
% (Disjointness of the two capability sets alone does NOT imply coverage:
% clause 3 is required, otherwise mdoc escapes both clauses 1 and 2.)

import vc_metamodel.
import governance_sources.

error governance_conflict(Credential c, Formatted_Credential f) <->
    EidasMandate::target(_, c),
    PrivacyRequirement::target(_, c),
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    conforms_vcdm(f),
    !supports_predicate_proof(f)
  ;
    EidasMandate::target(_, c),
    PrivacyRequirement::target(_, c),
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    supports_predicate_proof(f),
    !conforms_vcdm(f)
  ;
    EidasMandate::target(_, c),
    PrivacyRequirement::target(_, c),
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    !conforms_vcdm(f),
    !supports_predicate_proof(f).
